  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: linux-perf\n  version: \"7.2.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v${{ (version | split(\".\"))[0] }}.x/linux-${{ version }}.tar.xz\n  sha256: 7d0e7ce14f98c43efe880cffbf354a59be45928fdf7170d7333c374ae91c0d83\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - not linux\n    - ppc64le\n  dynamic_linking:\n    overlinking_behavior: error\n    overdepending_behavior: error\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    # perf links libstdc++ for the C++ demangler\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - make\n    - flex\n    - bison\n    - pkg-config\n  host:\n    - elfutils\n    # capstone provides the headers, libcapstone the lib and its run_exports\n    - capstone\n    - libcapstone\n    - libnuma\n    - libtraceevent\n    - slang\n    - liblzma-devel\n    - zlib\n    - zstd\n    - python\n    # CPython >= 3.14 ships libpython.so.1.0 in its own package rather than\n    # inside `python`; perf links it directly for its libpython support\n    - if: match(python, \">=3.14\")\n      then: libpython\n    - setuptools\n  run:\n    - python\n    - if: match(python, \">=3.14\")\n      then: libpython\n    - libnuma\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - perf version --build-options\n      # any of these features silently flipping to OFF (as the TUI did for\n      # every historical build of this feedstock) should fail the test\n      - 'for f in libtraceevent libslang libcapstone libelf dwarf debuginfod libpython libnuma zlib lzma zstd bpf aio; do perf version --build-options | grep -E \"$f: +\\[ on\" || { echo \"feature $f is not enabled\"; exit 1; }; done'\n      # enumerating events works without perf_event_open permissions\n      - 'perf list | grep -i \"cpu-clock\"'\n  - package_contents:\n      # strict: any packaged file not matched below fails the build\n      strict: true\n      bin:\n        - perf\n        - trace\n      include:\n        - perf/perf_dlfilter.h\n      files:\n        exists:\n          - bin/perf\n          - bin/trace\n          - etc/bash_completion.d/perf\n          - include/perf/perf_dlfilter.h\n          - libexec/perf-core/**\n          - share/doc/perf-tip/**\n\nabout:\n  summary: Performance analysis tools for Linux\n  description: |\n    Performance counters for Linux are a new kernel-based subsystem that\n    provide a framework for all things performance analysis. It covers hardware\n    level (CPU/PMU, Performance Monitoring Unit) features and software features\n    (software counters, tracepoints) as well.\n  license: GPL-2.0-only\n  license_file: LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0\n  homepage: https://www.kernel.org\n  documentation: https://docs.kernel.org/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - chrisburr\n",
